{{!-- BASIC-VIEW RAIL, as its own component so pages other than the dashboard can render it.
     /organizations was the first (2026-09-23): an org-unit supervisor reaches their rooms only
     through that page, and it had no rail at all.

     THIS IS A COPY OF THE DASHBOARD'S RAIL, NOT A MOVE (requested). The inline rail in
     components/dashboard/classic-view.hbs is untouched and still renders the Basic dashboard,
     so nothing about that page changed. The cost is real and worth stating plainly: there are
     now TWO copies of this markup, and a row added to one will not appear in the other. When
     you are ready, pointing classic-view.hbs at <Dashboard::ClassicRail /> deletes its copy
     and the duplication with it -- that is the only step left to finish the job.

     `@user` may be passed in to name whose rail this is; the dashboard resolves that from its
     own supervisee context. Left off, it falls back to the session user, which is what
     /organizations wants. Everything else the rail derives itself from services. --}}
{{!-- `ch-rail--org` marks the rail's ORG MODE (2026-09-25) -- see `orgSection` in the component.
     It is what the active-row treatment hangs off in _classic-home.scss, listed there beside
     `.ch-rail--account`'s, so the two rails say "you are here" the same way. The aria-label
     changes with it: in org mode this is not "your account" navigation. --}}
<aside class="ch-rail {{if this.isCollapsed "ch-rail--collapsed"}} {{if this.orgSection "ch-rail--org"}}" aria-label={{if this.orgSection (t "Organization navigation" key="classic_org_rail_aria") (t "Your account" key="classic_rail_aria")}}>

  {{!-- Identity — avatar + username, straight through to My Account. --}}
  <LinkTo @route="user.account" @model={{this.classicUser.user_name}} class="ch-rail__identity">
    <span class="ch-rail__avatar-wrap">
      <img src={{this.classicUser.avatar_url_with_fallback}} rel={{path "avatars/avatar-0.png"}} {{image-fallback-to-rel}} alt="" class="ch-rail__avatar">
      {{#if this.classicUser.online}}
        <span class="ch-rail__online" title={{t "currently online" key="currently_online"}}></span>
      {{/if}}
    </span>
    <span class="ch-rail__identity-text">
      {{!-- The name WRAPS in full rather than ellipsising, so it needs break points:
           `_` and `.` are class AL in UAX #14 and are not break opportunities on their
           own, so `marcus_willa` is one unbreakable run. `break-on-separators` inserts a
           <wbr> after each separator run, making the separator the preferred break and
           leaving the copied text identical. Paired with `overflow-wrap: break-word` on
           `.ch-rail__username`. Only this RENDERS the name — the `@model=` uses above
           pass it as a route segment and must stay raw. --}}
      <span class="ch-rail__username">{{break-on-separators this.classicUser.user_name}}</span>
      <span class="ch-rail__identity-sub">{{t "View my account" key="classic_view_my_account"}}</span>
    </span>
    <span class="ch-rail__arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
  </LinkTo>

  {{!-- Rail collapse control, sitting BETWEEN the account card and the first menu row.

       IN FLOW, not absolutely positioned. It used to be pinned to the aside's top-right
       corner, where it covered the account card. It cannot simply be given a fixed `top`
       to land on this boundary either: the account card's height VARIES now that a long
       username wraps to two lines, so any constant would drift off the seam. A flow
       element between the two lands on it at every height by construction.

       `.ch-rail__toggle-row` carries a negative right margin so the control straddles the
       rail's right border — half outside, half over the padding — see _classic-home.scss.

       A DISCLOSURE BUTTON, so `aria-expanded` is the whole contract — no `aria-controls`,
       which would have to point at an ancestor of this button or at a wrapper invented
       purely to be pointed at. Its accessible name CHANGES with state ("Collapse menu" /
       "Expand menu") rather than staying fixed, so a screen-reader user hears the action
       rather than the region. The label is `sr-only` text, not an `aria-label`, so it is
       translated through the same `{{t}}` pipeline as everything else on the page.
       Hidden below 901px — see the note on `.ch-rail--collapsed` in _classic-home.scss
       for why collapsing is a wide-screen affordance only. --}}
  <div class="ch-rail__toggle-row">
    <button type="button" class="ch-rail__toggle" aria-expanded={{if this.isCollapsed "false" "true"}} {{on "click" (this.ctrlAction "toggle_rail")}}>
      <svg class="ch-rail__toggle-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
        <polyline points="15 18 9 12 15 6"/>
      </svg>
      <span class="sr-only">
        {{#if this.isCollapsed}}
          {{t "Expand menu" key="classic_rail_expand"}}
        {{else}}
          {{t "Collapse menu" key="classic_rail_collapse"}}
        {{/if}}
      </span>
    </button>
  </div>

  <ul class="ch-rail__list">
    {{!-- ORDERED ALPHABETICALLY BY SUBJECT (requested 2026-09-23). Sorted on what each row
         is ABOUT, not on the title string it happens to render: several rows change their
         title with state -- Subscription shows "Tap here to update your subscription" or
         "Please update your license", Logging shows enabled/disabled, Sync has six -- so
         sorting on the visible text would reshuffle the rail at runtime.
         The identity/avatar button is not in this list; it sits above the rail as
         `.ch-rail__identity` and is deliberately excluded.
         Subjects, in order: Home Page, then Organizations (both pinned ahead of the
         alphabetical run, out of alphabetical order --
         requested 2026-09-24), then Create a New Board, Home Board, Logging, Subscription,
         Supervisors, Sync.
         (Organization Management was in this list until it was removed on 2026-09-24 -- see
         the note where it stood.)
         (Rooms was in this list until it was removed later the same day -- see the note
         where it stood.) --}}

    {{!-- TOUR ROW REMOVED FROM THE RAIL (requested 2026-09-23). This was the
         "Welcome! Take a tour" row; it is a closed access point, not a removed feature.
         The classic guided tour itself is untouched (utils/tours/classic-home.js, wired
         through utils/tours/registry.js) and is still offered by the "Let's Get Started"
         intro card further down this template, whose CTA calls the same `start_tour`.
         <GuidedTour /> also stays mounted in classic by
         app-navbar-authenticated-inner.hbs -- its own button is suppressed there, but the
         component is what listens for `auto_open_home_tour`, which `start_tour` sets, so
         unmounting it would break the intro card too (see the note at that mount site).
         The `tourAvailable` computed went with this row: it had no other consumer. --}}


    {{!-- NOTE: no supervisee list in the rail. Gen 2 kept the rail role-agnostic
         and put "People I Supervise" in the Communicators tab — verified against
         82a5b2dfc:templates/index/authenticated-new.hbs lines 1-310, which contain
         no `known_supervisees` reference. Listing them here too would duplicate
         the tab. --}}

    {{#unless this.onHomePage}}
      {{!-- HOME PAGE -- FIRST ROW UNDER THE DIVIDER (requested 2026-09-24: "add a Home Page
           card as the first button under the divider").
           THE RAIL IS NOT ONLY THE DASHBOARD'S any more. `dashboard/classic-rail` renders it on
           the Organizations page too, and from there Basic had no labelled way back to the
           dashboard -- the identity card above goes to the ACCOUNT page, which is a different
           place. This is the Basic counterpart of the Modern account rail's own Home Page row
           (components/account-rail.hbs:40), and it takes that row's route, label and two-tone
           house glyph so the two rails name the same destination the same way.
           UNGATED, unlike every other row here: every role has a home page.
           `@route="index"` rather than `user.home` for the same reason the Modern row uses it --
           `index` resolves to the signed-in user's own dashboard without this rail having to know
           whose name to put in the URL. --}}
      <li class="ch-rail__item">
        <LinkTo @route="index" class="ch-row ch-row--minor">
          <span class="ch-row__icon" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 10.5L12 3l9 7.5" stroke="#4C86D8"/><path d="M5 12v7a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h10a2 2 0 0 0 2-2v-7" stroke="#46505F"/></svg>
          </span>
          <span class="ch-row__short" aria-hidden="true">{{t "Home" key="home"}}</span>
          <span class="ch-row__body">
            <span class="ch-row__title">{{t "Home Page" key="home_page"}}</span>
          </span>
          <span class="ch-row__arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
        </LinkTo>
      </li>
    {{/unless}}

    {{!-- ORGANIZATIONS (added 2026-09-23). The rail already linked to INDIVIDUAL orgs
         below, but never to the list itself, so someone managing several had no way here
         to reach the Organizations page — only the org they happened to click. This is the
         Basic-view counterpart of the Modern pillnav's Organizations pill
         (components/user-pill-nav.hbs).
         GATED ON `has_management_responsibility`, the same gate the Modern pillnav uses, so
         the two views agree about who sees it. It was briefly widened to include supervisors
         and that was wrong: `/organizations/:id/people` wraps its entire contents in
         `permissions.edit`, so a supervisor following this row lands on "No information
         available". Supervisors get the Rooms row below instead, which goes somewhere they
         can actually use.
         FIRST IN THE RAIL as of 2026-09-24 (requested: "Position Organizations above Create
         a new board on the panel"). It is the one exception to the alphabetical ordering
         described at the top of this list, and deliberately so -- for an org manager this is
         the rail's primary destination, and alphabetical order buried it in the middle. --}}
    {{#if this.app_state.currentUser.has_management_responsibility}}
    <li class="ch-rail__item">
      {{!-- NOT HIGHLIGHTED IN ORG MODE (2026-09-25). It was, briefly: the request was "Show
           Organizations as the active button we are on", so this carried `is-active` whenever
           `orgSection` was true. On screen that lit TWO adjacent rows -- this one for the
           section, and the child row for the page you are actually on -- because every org page
           also lights its own row. Asked which should win, the answer was to keep this row and
           drop its highlight, so exactly one row is ever lit and it is the page you are on.
           THE ROW ITSELF STAYS, and that is the point of keeping it: it is the only way back to
           the org directory from the rail. `backRoute` on the tab strip leaves the org section
           entirely (to the app home), and the org switcher renders only for someone managing
           more than one org -- so removing this would have stranded single-org managers.
           <LinkTo>'s own active class still applies on `/organizations` itself, exactly as
           before org mode existed. --}}
      <LinkTo @route="organizations" class="ch-row ch-row--minor">
        <span class="ch-row__icon" aria-hidden="true">
          {{!-- Same building glyph the per-org rows below use, so the list and its entries
               read as one family. --}}
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="#46505F" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 22V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h8a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v18Z"/><path d="M6 12H4a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v6a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2"/><path d="M18 9h2a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v9a2 2 0 0 1-2 2h-2"/><path d="M10 6h4M10 10h4M10 14h4"/></svg>
        </span>
        <span class="ch-row__short" aria-hidden="true">{{t "Orgs" key="classic_short_orgs"}}</span>
        <span class="ch-row__body">
          <span class="ch-row__title">{{t "Organizations" key="organizations"}}</span>
          <span class="ch-row__sub">{{t "Your organizations, and the rooms inside them" key="classic_organizations_sub"}}</span>
        </span>
        <span class="ch-row__arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
      </LinkTo>
    </li>
    {{/if}}

    {{!-- ── THE SELECTED ORGANISATION'S OWN PAGES (2026-09-25, requested) ──────────────────
         Requested: "Then below the Organizations button add: Admin, Reports (the one for
         organizations, not the communicator stats page), Rooms, Trainings, Settings (the one for
         organizations, not the personal preferences)".

         BOTH DISAMBIGUATIONS ARE HONOURED BY THE ROUTE NAMES, which is the only place they can
         be: `organization.reports` is the org's report page, NOT `user.stats`; and
         `organization.settings` is the org's own settings, NOT `user.preferences`. Every row
         here is an `organization.*` route taking the org as its model, so none of them can
         resolve to a personal page.

         `@model={{this.org.id}}`, not the record: router.js declares this segment as
         `/organizations/:id` and every other org link in the app passes the id (see
         `templates/user/lessons.hbs` and the org switcher in `templates/organization.hbs`).

         ADMIN IS `organization.index`, the org's own management page. Stated because it is the
         one row whose target had to be inferred: there is also an `organization.extras` page
         whose heading is literally "Admin Actions", but it is gated on `this.model.admin` --
         the SITE-admin organisation -- so for every ordinary org that row would lead to a blank
         page. `index` is also the only one of the five that gives a way back to the org's own
         landing page, which a section nav missing it would not.

         `ch-row--minor` and the same two-tone glyph convention as every other row, so these read
         as part of the rail rather than as a panel bolted into it. --}}
    {{#if this.orgSection}}
      {{!-- NO ADMIN ROW (2026-09-25, requested: "the Admin tab needs to show as active when on
           the organizations index (so then remove the Admin button from the ch-rails menu)").
           `organization.index` is now the Admin TAB in the org strip (templates/organization.hbs),
           so a row here would be a second door to it sitting right beside the first. The four
           rows below are the org sections that strip does NOT carry. --}}
      <li class="ch-rail__item">
        <LinkTo @route="organization.reports" @model={{this.org.id}} @activeClass="is-active" class="ch-row ch-row--minor">
          <span class="ch-row__icon" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 3v18h18" stroke="#46505F"/><path d="M18 9l-5 5-2-2-4 4" stroke="#2A9D8F"/></svg>
          </span>
          <span class="ch-row__short" aria-hidden="true">{{t "Reports" key="reports"}}</span>
          <span class="ch-row__body"><span class="ch-row__title">{{t "Reports" key="reports"}}</span></span>
          <span class="ch-row__arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
        </LinkTo>
      </li>
      {{!-- Rooms takes `is-active` from <LinkTo> on the LIST route, and `@current-when` adds the
           room DETAIL page: `organization.room` is a SIBLING of `organization.rooms` in
           router.js (`path: '/rooms/:room_id'`), so the path nests but the route name does not
           and the parent row would otherwise sit dark while you stand on a room. Same trap the
           account rail documents for Goals and Logs. --}}
      <li class="ch-rail__item">
        <LinkTo @route="organization.rooms" @model={{this.org.id}} @activeClass="is-active" @current-when="organization.rooms organization.room" class="ch-row ch-row--minor">
          <span class="ch-row__icon" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="16" rx="2" stroke="#46505F"/><path d="M3 10h18" stroke="#46505F"/><path d="M9 20v-6h6v6" stroke="#2A9D8F"/></svg>
          </span>
          <span class="ch-row__short" aria-hidden="true">{{t "Rooms" key="rooms"}}</span>
          <span class="ch-row__body"><span class="ch-row__title">{{t "Rooms" key="rooms"}}</span></span>
          <span class="ch-row__arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
        </LinkTo>
      </li>
      <li class="ch-rail__item">
        <LinkTo @route="organization.lessons" @model={{this.org.id}} @activeClass="is-active" class="ch-row ch-row--minor">
          {{!-- The mortarboard the account rail and the Trainings page header both use, so this
               destination is drawn the same way wherever it is offered. --}}
          <span class="ch-row__icon" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 8.5 12 4l9 4.5-9 4.5Z" stroke="#46505F"/><path d="M7 11v5c0 1.5 2.2 2.5 5 2.5s5-1 5-2.5v-5" stroke="#2A9D8F"/></svg>
          </span>
          <span class="ch-row__short" aria-hidden="true">{{t "Training" key="classic_short_trainings"}}</span>
          <span class="ch-row__body"><span class="ch-row__title">{{t "Trainings" key="trainings"}}</span></span>
          <span class="ch-row__arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
        </LinkTo>
      </li>
      <li class="ch-rail__item">
        <LinkTo @route="organization.settings" @model={{this.org.id}} @activeClass="is-active" class="ch-row ch-row--minor">
          <span class="ch-row__icon" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3" stroke="#2A9D8F"/><path d="M19.4 15a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 .33 1.82l.06.06a2 2 0 1 1-2.83 2.83l-.06-.06a1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1.82-.33 1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1 1.51V21a2 2 0 1 1-4 0v-.09A1.65 1.65 0 0 0 9 19.4a1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1.82.33l-.06.06a2 2 0 1 1-2.83-2.83l.06-.06a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 .33-1.82 1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1.51-1H3a2 2 0 1 1 0-4h.09A1.65 1.65 0 0 0 4.6 9a1.65 1.65 0 0 0-.33-1.82l-.06-.06a2 2 0 1 1 2.83-2.83l.06.06A1.65 1.65 0 0 0 9 4.6a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 1-1.51V3a2 2 0 1 1 4 0v.09a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 1 1.51 1.65 1.65 0 0 0 1.82-.33l.06-.06a2 2 0 1 1 2.83 2.83l-.06.06a1.65 1.65 0 0 0-.33 1.82V9a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 1.51 1H21a2 2 0 1 1 0 4h-.09a1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1.51 1Z" stroke="#46505F"/></svg>
          </span>
          <span class="ch-row__short" aria-hidden="true">{{t "Settings" key="settings"}}</span>
          <span class="ch-row__body"><span class="ch-row__title">{{t "Settings" key="settings"}}</span></span>
          <span class="ch-row__arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
        </LinkTo>
      </li>
    {{/if}}

    {{!-- ── THE PERSONAL DASHBOARD ROWS, HIDDEN IN ORG MODE (2026-09-25, requested: "Hide the
         buttons shown in the attachment") ────────────────────────────────────────────────
         The attachment named four -- Create a New Board, Home Board, Logging and Sync -- and
         this `{{#unless}}` spans SIX, because Subscription and Supervisors sit between them in
         source order and are the same kind of row: your account, not this organisation's. They
         did not render for the account in the screenshot (both are gated), which is why they
         were not in it. Leaving them would have stranded two personal rows in the middle of an
         org nav. Say the word and either comes back -- it is where this `{{#unless}}` starts and
         stops, nothing else. --}}
    {{#unless this.orgSection}}

    {{!-- Available to every role in the original. --}}
    <li class="ch-rail__item">
      <button type="button" class="ch-row ch-row--minor" {{on "click" (this.ctrlAction "newBoard")}}>
        <span class="ch-row__icon" aria-hidden="true">
          {{!-- Two-tone, and the SAME board-plus glyph the Actions tab's New Board
               tile uses (ch-tile--create): charcoal board, teal plus. --}}
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="2.5" y="4" width="12.5" height="15" rx="2" stroke="#46505F"/><line x1="2.5" y1="8.5" x2="15" y2="8.5" stroke="#46505F"/><line x1="20" y1="14.5" x2="20" y2="21.5" stroke="#2A9D8F"/><line x1="16.5" y1="18" x2="23.5" y2="18" stroke="#2A9D8F"/></svg>
        </span>
        <span class="ch-row__short" aria-hidden="true">{{t "New" key="classic_short_new"}}</span>
        <span class="ch-row__body">
          <span class="ch-row__title">{{t "Create a New Board" key="create_a_new_board"}}</span>
        </span>
        <span class="ch-row__arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
      </button>
    </li>

    {{!-- Home board: open it, wait on the copy, or go pick one. --}}
    <li class="ch-rail__item">
      {{#if this.homeBoardKey}}
        <LinkTo @route="board" @model={{this.homeBoardKey}} class="ch-row ch-row--board">
          <span class="ch-row__icon" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="#2A9D8F" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 10.5L12 3l9 7.5"/><path d="M5 12v7a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h10a2 2 0 0 0 2-2v-7"/></svg>
          </span>
          <span class="ch-row__short" aria-hidden="true">{{t "Home" key="classic_short_home"}}</span>
          <span class="ch-row__body">
            <span class="ch-row__title">{{t "Home Board" key="home_board"}}</span>
            <span class="ch-row__sub">{{this.homeBoardKey}}</span>
          </span>
          <span class="ch-row__arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
        </LinkTo>
      {{else if this.homeBoardPending}}
        <span class="ch-row ch-row--board ch-row--static">
          <span class="ch-row__icon" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="#2A9D8F" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 10.5L12 3l9 7.5"/><path d="M5 12v7a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h10a2 2 0 0 0 2-2v-7"/></svg>
          </span>
          <span class="ch-row__short" aria-hidden="true">{{t "Home" key="classic_short_home"}}</span>
          <span class="ch-row__body">
            <span class="ch-row__title">{{t "Home Board" key="home_board"}}</span>
            <span class="ch-row__sub">{{t "copying %{brd}..." key="copying_board" brd=this.classicUser.home_board_pending}}</span>
          </span>
        </span>
      {{else}}
        <LinkTo @route="board-picker" class="ch-row ch-row--board ch-row--todo">
          <span class="ch-row__icon" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="#2A9D8F" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 10.5L12 3l9 7.5"/><path d="M5 12v7a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h10a2 2 0 0 0 2-2v-7"/></svg>
          </span>
          <span class="ch-row__short" aria-hidden="true">{{t "Home" key="classic_short_home"}}</span>
          <span class="ch-row__body">
            <span class="ch-row__title">{{t "You haven't set a home board yet" key="choose_home_board"}}</span>
            <span class="ch-row__sub">{{t "Let us help you choose one." key="let_us_help_choose_home"}}</span>
          </span>
          <span class="ch-row__arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
        </LinkTo>
      {{/if}}
    </li>

    {{!-- Logging. Off -> Usage Reports (where the enable button lives).
         On -> notifications + recent sessions. --}}
    <li class="ch-rail__item">
      {{#if this.loggingEnabled}}
        <button type="button" class="ch-row ch-row--logging ch-row--logging-on" {{on "click" (this.ctrlAction "load_sessions")}}>
          <span class="ch-row__icon" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="#4C86D8" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M8 6h13"/><path d="M8 12h13"/><path d="M8 18h13"/><path d="M3 6h.01"/><path d="M3 12h.01"/><path d="M3 18h.01"/></svg>
          </span>
          <span class="ch-row__short" aria-hidden="true">{{t "Logging" key="classic_short_logging"}}</span>
          <span class="ch-row__body">
            {{#if this.loggingWithGeo}}
              <span class="ch-row__title">{{t "Logging is enabled" key="classic_logging_full"}}</span>
            {{else}}
              <span class="ch-row__title">{{t "Logging is enabled (no geo)" key="classic_logging_no_geo"}}</span>
            {{/if}}
            <span class="ch-row__sub">{{t "Notifications & recent sessions" key="classic_notifications_and_sessions"}}</span>
          </span>
          <span class="ch-row__arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
        </button>
      {{else}}
        <button type="button" class="ch-row ch-row--logging ch-row--todo" {{on "click" (this.ctrlAction "load_reports")}}>
          <span class="ch-row__icon" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="#46505F" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M8 6h13"/><path d="M8 12h13"/><path d="M8 18h13"/><path d="M3 6h.01"/><path d="M3 12h.01"/><path d="M3 18h.01"/></svg>
          </span>
          <span class="ch-row__short" aria-hidden="true">{{t "Logging" key="classic_short_logging"}}</span>
          <span class="ch-row__body">
            <span class="ch-row__title">{{t "Logging is disabled" key="classic_logging_disabled"}}</span>
            <span class="ch-row__sub">{{t "Turn on reports to see your usage" key="classic_logging_disabled_sub"}}</span>
          </span>
          <span class="ch-row__arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
        </button>
      {{/if}}
    </li>


    {{!-- NO ORGANIZATION MANAGEMENT ROW HERE (removed 2026-09-24, requested: "remove
         organization management from ch-rail, since we already have organizations as a button
         there").
         It used to render one chip per managed org, or a single "Organization Management" row
         when there was only one, both linking to `organization`. The Organizations row further
         down goes to `organizations`, which lists exactly those orgs and opens any of them -- so
         this was a second door to the same place, and on a rail whose rows are meant to be one
         per destination.
         A CLOSED ACCESS POINT, NOT A REMOVED FEATURE: nothing about org management changed, and
         the `organization` route is reached in one more click. --}}
    {{!-- ROOMS -- THE SLP-ONLY HALF OF A PAIR (2026-09-23). Rooms and Organizations are
         mutually exclusive on this rail: someone who MANAGES an org gets the Organizations
         row above and reaches their rooms through that page, and someone who only SUPERVISES
         gets this direct link instead, because the Organizations page is manager-gated
         (templates/organization/people.hbs:1 wraps the whole thing in `permissions.edit`) and
         would be a dead end for them.
         That is why the gate is `unless has_management_responsibility` and not merely
         `if roomsAllOrgId` -- a manager with rooms would otherwise get both rows.

         list of the rooms themselves (2026-09-02, requested): it goes to the user's
         Rooms page and lets that page do the listing.
         `roomsAllOrgId` and `sortedRooms` are INHERITED from
         authenticated-view.js — the modern Rooms card's "see all" button resolves
         the destination the same way (first supervised unit's organization_id), so
         the two cannot drift. Guarded on `roomsAllOrgId` as well as the units
         themselves: a unit with no organization_id would otherwise build a LinkTo
         with an undefined model. --}}
    {{#unless this.app_state.currentUser.has_management_responsibility}}
    {{#if this.roomsAllOrgId}}
    <li class="ch-rail__item">
      <LinkTo @route="organization.rooms" @model={{this.roomsAllOrgId}} class="ch-row ch-row--rooms">
        <span class="ch-row__icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 21V6a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h9a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v15" stroke="#46505F"/><path d="M14 10h6a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v10" stroke="#46505F"/><line x1="2" y1="21" x2="22" y2="21" stroke="#46505F"/><rect x="6" y="9" width="2.6" height="2.6" rx="0.5" fill="#2A9D8F" stroke="none"/><rect x="6" y="14" width="2.6" height="2.6" rx="0.5" fill="#2A9D8F" stroke="none"/></svg>
        </span>
        <span class="ch-row__short" aria-hidden="true">{{t "Rooms" key="classic_short_rooms"}}</span>
        <span class="ch-row__body">
          <span class="ch-row__title">{{t "Rooms" key="rooms"}}</span>
          <span class="ch-row__sub">{{t "room" count=this.sortedRooms.length key="slp_rooms"}}</span>
        </span>
        <span class="ch-row__arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
      </LinkTo>
    </li>
    {{/if}}
    {{/unless}}

    {{!-- ROOMS ROW REMOVED FROM THE RAIL (requested 2026-09-23). A closed access point,
         not a removed feature: the Rooms page is unchanged and still reachable from the
         organization nav (templates/organization.hbs -> `organization.rooms`) and from
         the Modern dashboard's "view all" link (dashboard/authenticated-view.hbs).
         Nothing was orphaned by this. `roomsAllOrgId` and `sortedRooms` are defined on
         the PARENT class (dashboard/authenticated-view.js) and this template only
         inherited them, so both still have their Modern consumers; and no `.ch-row--rooms`
         rule exists in the stylesheets, so there is no dead CSS either. Both checked. --}}

    {{!-- Subscription state. Same gate as the original: only when the
         subscriptions feature is on AND the account is expired or in its grace
         period, so a healthy paid account sees nothing here. --}}
    {{#if this.app_state.feature_flags.subscriptions}}
      {{#if this.app_state.currentUser.expired_or_grace_period}}
      <li class="ch-rail__item">
        <LinkTo @route="user.subscription" @model={{this.classicUser.user_name}} class="ch-row ch-row--todo">
          <span class="ch-row__icon" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="#C0392B" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12" y2="13"/><line x1="12" y1="16" x2="12.01" y2="16"/></svg>
          </span>
          <span class="ch-row__short" aria-hidden="true">{{t "Account" key="classic_short_account"}}</span>
          <span class="ch-row__body">
            {{#if this.app_state.currentUser.expired}}
              <span class="ch-row__title">{{t "Tap here to update your subscription" key="tap_to_subscribe"}}</span>
              <span class="ch-row__sub">{{t "your free preview has ended" key="preview_expired"}}</span>
            {{else}}
              <span class="ch-row__title">{{t "Please update your license" key="update_license"}}</span>
              <span class="ch-row__sub">{{t "your free preview ends" key="preview_expires"}} {{date this.app_state.currentUser.subscription.expires "day"}}</span>
            {{/if}}
          </span>
          <span class="ch-row__arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
        </LinkTo>
      </li>
      {{/if}}
    {{/if}}

    {{!-- Supervisors — opens the Supervision settings modal for this user.
         Communicators only: a supporter's own team is the supervisee list above,
         which is the same split the original made. --}}
    {{#unless this.app_state.currentUser.supporter_role}}
    <li class="ch-rail__item">
      <button type="button" class="ch-row ch-row--sup" {{on "click" (this.ctrlAction "manage_supervisors")}}>
        <span class="ch-row__icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="#4C86D8" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M17 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H5a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"/><circle cx="9" cy="7" r="4"/><path d="M23 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87"/><path d="M16 3.13a4 4 0 0 1 0 7.75"/></svg>
        </span>
        <span class="ch-row__short" aria-hidden="true">{{t "Team" key="classic_short_team"}}</span>
        <span class="ch-row__body">
          {{#if this.hasSupervisors}}
            <span class="ch-row__title">{{t "supervisor" count=this.supervisorCount key="classic_supervisor_count"}}</span>
            <span class="ch-row__sub">{{t "Manage who supports you" key="classic_manage_supervisors_sub"}}</span>
          {{else}}
            <span class="ch-row__title">{{t "No Supervisors" key="no_supervisors"}}</span>
            <span class="ch-row__sub">{{t "Add someone to support you" key="classic_add_supervisor_sub"}}</span>
          {{/if}}
        </span>
        <span class="ch-row__arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
      </button>
    </li>
    {{/unless}}

    {{!-- Offline sync — LAST in the rail (2026-09-02, requested). Kept on this
         page because offline readiness is not surfaced anywhere else, but it is a
         background concern rather than a destination, so it sits below the
         navigation rows. Gated on `sync_able` (extras ready + no external device)
         exactly as the modern dashboard gates it. --}}
    {{#if this.sync_able}}
    <li class="ch-rail__item">
      <button type="button" class="ch-row ch-row--sync" {{on "click" (this.ctrlAction "sync")}}>
        <span class="ch-row__icon {{if (persistence-value 'syncing') "ch-row__icon--spinning"}}" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="#2A9D8F" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="23 4 23 10 17 10"/><polyline points="1 20 1 14 7 14"/><path d="M3.51 9a9 9 0 0 1 14.85-3.36L23 10M1 14l4.64 4.36A9 9 0 0 0 20.49 15"/></svg>
        </span>
        <span class="ch-row__short" aria-hidden="true">{{t "Sync" key="classic_short_sync"}}</span>
        <span class="ch-row__body">
          {{#if (persistence-value 'sync_succeeded')}}
            <span class="ch-row__title">{{t "Sync Done!" key="sync_done"}}</span>
            <span class="ch-row__sub">{{t "Synced and ready for offline" key="up_to_date"}}</span>
          {{else if (persistence-value 'sync_failed')}}
            <span class="ch-row__title">{{t "Sync Failed, see details below" key="sync_failed"}}</span>
            <span class="ch-row__sub">{{persistence-value 'sync_status_error'}}</span>
          {{else if (persistence-value 'syncing')}}
            <span class="ch-row__title">{{t "Syncing..." key="syncing_ellipsis"}}</span>
            {{#if (persistence-value 'sync_progress.total')}}
              <span class="ch-row__sub">{{persistence-value 'sync_progress.visited'}} / {{t "board" key="communication_set_board" count=(persistence-value 'sync_progress.total')}}</span>
            {{else}}
              <span class="ch-row__sub">{{t "initializing..." key="initializing_lower"}}</span>
            {{/if}}
          {{else if this.needs_sync}}
            {{#if this.app_state.installed_app}}
              <span class="ch-row__title">{{t "Sync before going offline!" key="needs_update"}}</span>
            {{else}}
              <span class="ch-row__title">{{t "Sync if planning to go offline" key="sync_if_planning_offline"}}</span>
            {{/if}}
            <span class="ch-row__sub">{{t "Save your boards for offline use" key="classic_sync_sub"}}</span>
          {{else}}
            <span class="ch-row__title">{{t "Synced and ready for offline" key="up_to_date"}}</span>
            <span class="ch-row__sub">{{t "Sync again any time" key="classic_sync_again"}}</span>
          {{/if}}
        </span>
        <span class="ch-row__arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
      </button>
    </li>
    {{/if}}
    {{/unless}}{{!-- ...end of the personal dashboard rows; see the note where this opens --}}

  </ul>

  {{!-- Rail footer — the small utility links the original kept below the list. --}}
  <div class="ch-rail__footer">
    <a href="#" class="ch-rail__minor" {{on "click" (this.ctrlAction "reload")}}>
      {{!-- Two-tone circular arrow, matching the icon set on the tiles above:
           charcoal ring, teal arrowhead. --}}
      <svg class="ch-rail__minor-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
        <path d="M20.5 12a8.5 8.5 0 1 1-2.49-6.01" stroke="#46505F"/>
        <polyline points="20.5 3.5 20.5 9 15 9" stroke="#2A9D8F"/>
      </svg>
      {{t "Reload" key="reload"}}
    </a>
    {{#if (persistence-value 'sync_log')}}
      <a href="#" class="ch-rail__minor" {{on "click" (this.ctrlAction "sync_details")}}>
        <svg class="ch-rail__minor-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M4 4.5h11l4 4V19a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H5a1 1 0 0 1-1-1z" stroke="#46505F"/>
          <line x1="8" y1="13" x2="15" y2="13" stroke="#2A9D8F"/>
        </svg>
        {{t "recent sync details log" key="recent_sync_details"}}
      </a>
    {{/if}}
  </div>
</aside>
